## TypeScript Standards

### Strict Rules (Never Violate)
- No `any` — use `unknown` and narrow with type guards
- No non-null assertion `!` — handle nulls explicitly
- All async functions return typed promises
- Use Zod schemas for runtime validation of external data
- Prefer `const` over `let` unless reassignment is required
- No unused variables or imports

### Patterns

#### Error Handling
```typescript
// ✅ Good
const result = await userService.getUser(id)
if (result.error) throw new AppError('USER_NOT_FOUND', result.error)

// ❌ Bad
const user = await getUser(id)  // untyped, no error handling
```

#### Component Props
```typescript
// ✅ Good
interface ProfileCardProps {
  userId: string
  onError?: (error: Error) => void
}

// ❌ Bad
const ProfileCard = (props: any) => { ... }
```

#### Named Exports Only
- Use named exports for all components, hooks, utils, and types
- Default exports are ONLY for Expo Router screen files

### File Organization
- One component (or hook, util, type) per file
- Barrel exports (`index.ts`) for feature directories
- Keep files under 300 lines; split into sub-modules when exceeded